      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224552/assets/182a88f3f8f379dd35228cbb6ebe5c34d9761608a6a222710f50d8f272d3cf1e.png)\n\nCalculate $\\operatorname{cos}⁡R.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall the definition of cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡R=\\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}=\\frac{QR}{PR}=\\frac{2}{PR}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing length $PR.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PR & =\\sqrt{P{Q}^{2}+Q{R}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡R & =\\frac{2}{PR}=\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
